ineages into `research/research.md` (agreement, disagreement, unique evidence)\nspecs/sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening/tasks.md:50:- [x] T005 Add the hook-flags resolver and parser, then rewrite `checkSuppression` to merge environment over file with per-value sources, the two aliases and a source-specific repair. Test with the master switch in a fixture `hook-flags.env` and absent from the environment, plus an empty environment value overriding a truthy file value (the battery and the suite, REQ-001) [EVIDENCE: tests \"a master switch saved in hook-flags.env fails suppression and names its line\" and \"hook-flags.env parsing matches the hooks: BOM, quotes, trailing comment and HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG\". Mutation: old `checkSuppression` made 3 tests fail]\nspecs/sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening/tasks.md:51:- [x] T006 Make `registersAdvisory` event- and matcher-aware per runtime. Move the Codex fixture from `SessionStart` to `PreToolUse` with matcher `exec|Bash`, and add for each of Claude, Codex, Devin and Cursor a real-shape PASS, a wrong-event FAIL and a wrong-matcher FAIL (the battery and the suite, REQ-002) [EVIDENCE: test \"ai-tool-hooks accepts each runtime's real wiring and refuses a wrong event or matcher\", 12 runs over four real configs. Mutation A, the old substring match, failed it at the wrong event. Mutation B, the matcher check replaced by `return true`, failed it at \"claude: a matcher that misses the shell tool must not count\"]\nspecs/sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening/tasks.md:52:- [x] T007 Correct the Claude and Codex rows of section 3 to the wiring T006 enforces: Claude matcher `Bash`, Codex matcher `exec|Bash` (`.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/README.md`, REQ-002) [EVIDENCE: diff of `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/README.md` changes only the Claude and Codex Event cells to matcher `Bash` and matcher `exec\\|Bash`, column count unchanged]\nspecs/sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening/tasks.md:55:- [x] T008 Gates row: UNKNOWN with no repair for a helper error, an unparsable report or a report without `gates`. DEGRADED with `/doctor:git hooks` for a saved-off gate. Drop `GATE_REGISTRY` from the helper's environment. One test per case (the battery and the suite, REQ-004) [EVIDENCE: tests \"gates reports UNKNOWN with no repair when the helper fails or its report has no gates\", \"a gate saved off degrades the run to exit 3 with the hooks repair\" and \"gates ignores a GATE_REGISTRY inherited from the environment\". Mutation A, old `checkGates`, failed 3. Mutation B, `GATE_REGISTRY` kept, failed the last one]\nspecs/sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening/tasks.md:56:- [x] T009 AI-tool row: UNKNOWN with a `--tool` hint when no tool is active and nothing is broken, plus OpenCode and Pi content anchors. Tests for a tool-less run and for OpenCode and Pi files without their anchors (the battery and the suite, REQ-005) [EVIDENCE: tests \"a run with no active tool and nothing broken is UNKNOWN and names --tool\" and \"opencode and pi pass only when the adapter registers its event and imports git-rule-checks.mjs\". Mutation: old row failed 3 tests. A tool-less run outside Claude Code on this checkout exits 3]\nspecs/sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening/tasks.md:57:- [x] T010 Worktree row: judge the base itself, fail a file at the base, and name the winning source in the repair. Tests for an existing unwritable base, a file at the base path and an environment-sourced base (the battery and the suite, REQ-006) [EVIDENCE: test \"worktrees fails an unwritable base and a file at the base, and names the variable that set it\". Mutation: old `checkWorktrees` failed it]\nspecs/sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening/tasks.md:60:- [x] T011 Install repair: name each missing path in a `git -C <own checkout> restore --source=HEAD -- <path>` command, or reinstalling when the root is not a git work tree. Drop bare `/doctor:update` (the battery and the suite, REQ-008) [EVIDENCE: tests \"install names a repair that restores missing sk-git files\" and \"install restores exactly the missing path of a git install root, and the restore turns the row PASS\". Mutation: old `INSTALL_REPAIR` failed both]\nspecs/sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening/tasks.md:61:- [x] T012 Standards repair: for the missing `skgit.contractDir` case, name `git config --<scope> --unset skgit.contractDir` with the scope read through `--show-scope`, or creating the directory. Keep `/doctor:git standards` for a malformed block (the battery and the suite, REQ-009) [EVIDENCE: tests \"standards fails a missing configured contract dir and reports an absent contract\", which applies the printed unset, and \"standards names the global scope when the missing contract dir is set globally\". Mutation: old repair failed both. The malformed block keeps `/doctor:git standards`]\nspecs/sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening/tasks.md:62:- [x] T013 Hooks repair per option A: when the inspected repository shares this checkout's git common dir, name `bash <this checkout's root>/scripts/install-git-hooks.sh` by absolute path. Otherwise name `git config core.hooksPath <this checkout's root>/scripts/git-hooks`. Never name the inspected repository's installer. Tests assert both strings, including a foreign fixture that carries the toolchain sentinel (the battery and the suite, REQ-007) [EVIDENCE: tests \"hooks accepts links into the repository's own hook sources and names a repair that exists\", which asserts a sentinel clone still gets `core.hooksPath`, \"hooks names this checkout's installer by absolute path when the inspected repository is the battery's own checkout\" and \"a foreign repository applying the printed core.hooksPath repair turns hooks PASS\". Mutation: the old `repoTree` repair failed the first two]\nspecs/sk-git/033